Extraction and capture collapses our online platforms, ever impoverishing us, moving us towards digital serfdom.
</p>
        <p><time datetime="2026-08-30" title="2026-08-30">This morning</time> with coffee in hand, I pulled up my <span><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RSS">Rich Site Summary</a></span> (<abbr title="Rich Site Summary">RSS</abbr> <small><a class="ref" rel="tag opener" aria-label="Other site-wide references of “Rich Site Summary”" title="Other site-wide references of “Rich Site Summary”" href="https://takeonrules.com/site-map/glossary/#abbr-dfn-GLOSSARY-RSS">&#128214;</a></small>)
 feed and read.  A few posts
in I read <a href="https://brandons-journal.com/post/blogger-will-most-likely-be-the-next-geocities">Appreciate Blogger While You Can</a>.  This struck a deep nerve.</p>
<p>We live in an era of ever encroaching light pollution.  The night skies of
centuries ago are different from what the night skies most of us experience
these days.  As light pollution encroaches, once faint stars disappear.</p>
<p>I’ve been blogging since <time datetime="2011-02-02" title="2011-02-02">2011</time>.  I’ve witnessed moving towards platforms that
invariably collapse once capital has extracted and strip-mined their value.  I
read of folks lambasting Google+ but for the <span><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Role-playing_game">Role Playing Game</a></span> (<abbr title="Role Playing Game">RPG</abbr> <small><a class="ref" rel="tag opener" aria-label="Other site-wide references of “Role Playing Game”" title="Other site-wide references of “Role Playing Game”" href="https://takeonrules.com/site-map/glossary/#abbr-dfn-GLOSSARY-RPG">&#128214;</a></small>)
 scene, this was the platform
where conversation, experimentation, and play happened.</p>
<p>And when Google sunset Google+, there was no obvious successor.  And folks
scattered.  Finding the odd and unique has become harder.  And the state of
connection, more precarious, as capital seeks to create walled gardens (waves at
Discord and Facebook) while also assaulting the open (hello aggressive
<span>Large Language Model</span> (<abbr title="Large Language Model">LLM</abbr> <small><a class="ref" rel="tag opener" aria-label="Other site-wide references of “Large Language Model”" title="Other site-wide references of “Large Language Model”" href="https://takeonrules.com/site-map/glossary/#abbr-dfn-GLOSSARY-LLM">&#128214;</a></small>)
-feeding agents)</p>
<p><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metcalfe%27s_law">Metcalfe&rsquo;s law</a> states: “the financial value or influence of a telecommunications
network is proportional to the square of the number of connected users of the
system (n^2).”</p>
<p>The open internet struggles to survive the assault of capital because the value
is not directly something that can be captured.  There is a concerted effort to
induce internet serfdom.  And as Brandon says, appreciate blogger while you
still can, because anyone that’s watched Google knows that it will end that
product.</p>
<p>The stars that I see twinkling on the internet are one light pollution event
away from disappearing.  The night sky will be the poorer for their absence, but
at least the shareholder’s valuation will increase.</p>

